{"data":{"list":[{"author":"claude","facet":"html","label":"the agent plugin payload (cluster)","new":"<!-- agentmodules — the agent add-on's PLUGIN payload: a cluster control\n     whose divs install the notebook modules headless (each is flagged\n     `module: true`; api.js registers them on the page). Registered with\n     the Development app through runtime/dev/plugins.json (the platform's\n     per-instance plugin mechanism, dev.plugins) — target dev.dev, so the\n     boot's plugin pass installs this BEFORE the frame mounts and the\n     session's presence checks see the modules. Nothing in the dev app\n     names the agent; this control + one registry entry ARE the plugin. -->\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n","old":"","patch_id":"p1","time":1785424359576},{"author":"claude","facet":"html","label":"memory v0: memory joins the cluster","new":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","old":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>","patch_id":"p2","time":1785504784926},{"author":"Claude","facet":"html","label":"cluster: install the ask socket adapter","new":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:ask\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","old":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","patch_id":"p3","time":1786366320851},{"author":"Claude","facet":"html","label":"the ask socket module retires (askrow/describebtn graft instead)","new":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","old":"<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:ask\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","patch_id":"p4","time":1786367784008},{"author":"Claude","facet":"html","label":"the cluster is the whole payload (one registry entry)","new":"<!-- agentmodules — the agent add-on's ENTIRE plugin payload: ONE\n     runtime/dev/plugins.json entry (target dev.dev) installs this\n     cluster at boot, and it brings everything else itself. The module\n     divs register the shared modules headless (each flagged\n     `module: true`; api.js registers them on the page); the describebtn\n     child arms the workbench's desc drafter (a document-level listener,\n     no DOM of its own); and this control's js grafts the chat surface\n     into the notebook's plugin slot whenever one appears. Nothing in\n     the dev app names the agent; this control + one registry entry ARE\n     the plugin. -->\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:describebtn\" hidden></div>","old":"<!-- agentmodules — the agent add-on's PLUGIN payload: a cluster control\n     whose divs install the notebook modules headless (each is flagged\n     `module: true`; api.js registers them on the page). Registered with\n     the Development app through runtime/dev/plugins.json (the platform's\n     per-instance plugin mechanism, dev.plugins) — target dev.dev, so the\n     boot's plugin pass installs this BEFORE the frame mounts and the\n     session's presence checks see the modules. Nothing in the dev app\n     names the agent; this control + one registry entry ARE the plugin. -->\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentloop\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:agentprompt\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"data-control\" data-control=\"agent:memory\" hidden></div>","patch_id":"p5","time":1786368728231},{"author":"Claude","facet":"js","label":"graft the chat surface from the cluster","new":"// agentmodules js — the graft arm of the one-entry plugin. The session\n// mounts its notebook lazily, so the chat surface can't be a static\n// child here: this script watches for the notebook's plugin slot\n// (.ss-plugins) and installs agent.askrow into it whenever an unclaimed\n// one appears — including remounts. The marker it sets is the same one\n// the loader's registry pass uses, so the two mechanisms can coexist\n// without double-mounting on an instance that carries extra entries.\n(function () {\n  if (document.__nbAgentAskGraft) return;\n  document.__nbAgentAskGraft = true;\n  if (typeof installControl !== \"function\") return;\n  var graft = function () {\n    var slot = document.querySelector(\".ss-plugins:not([data-nb-plugin])\");\n    if (!slot) return;\n    slot.dataset.nbPlugin = \"agent-askrow\";\n    installControl(slot, \"agent\", \"askrow\", null);\n  };\n  graft();\n  new MutationObserver(graft).observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });\n})();","old":"","patch_id":"p6","time":1786368728239}]},"id":"ogmwzx19fb395b095w0_patches","readers":[],"time":1786368728239,"username":"system","writers":[]}